<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prophezei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">founded 1525</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Prophezei was a school of biblical study founded in Zürich in 1525 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huldrych-zwingli">Huldrych Zwingli</a> in place of the old chapter school of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grossmunster">Grossmünster</a>. Clergy and students met daily to read scripture in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a>, Greek and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> and to expound it in German. It trained Reformed ministers, produced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zurich-bible">Zürich Bible</a> and was a forerunner of the University of Zürich.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prophezei.jpg" alt="Prophezei" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roland zh · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Z%C3%BCrich_-_Grossm%C3%BCnster_-_Grossm%C3%BCnsterplatz_IMG_4287_ShiftN.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
